WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.006 --> 00:00:04.995
- All right, so we're gonna
talk about fat burning foods.

00:00:04.995 --> 00:00:08.585
There are actually two sets of hormones.

00:00:08.585 --> 00:00:10.762
Those are hormones that
trigger fat burning,

00:00:10.762 --> 00:00:12.062
and them there are hormones

00:00:12.062 --> 00:00:14.365
that trigger fat storing,

00:00:14.365 --> 00:00:19.003
and this principle really
comes into play as you age,

00:00:19.003 --> 00:00:21.505
because when you're young,
you have a good metabolism,

00:00:21.505 --> 00:00:22.998
you could pretty much
get away with anything.

00:00:22.998 --> 00:00:25.413
But, when you age, you have
to consider the hormones.

00:00:25.413 --> 00:00:28.055
So we want to go away
from the calorie counting

00:00:28.055 --> 00:00:31.812
and focus more on how foods
influence the hormone effects.

00:00:31.812 --> 00:00:33.966
I'm going to just cover
some real key points here.

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:37.061
Number one, protein, all right?

00:00:37.061 --> 00:00:39.092
If you have the right amount of protein,

00:00:39.092 --> 00:00:42.236
which is three to four ounces per meal,

00:00:42.236 --> 00:00:44.225
you will trigger the fat burning process.

00:00:44.225 --> 00:00:46.428
That's why skipping a meal,
especially for breakfast,

00:00:46.428 --> 00:00:48.690
is not a good thing, because
you're not triggering

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.872
any fat burning, you're
actually starving your body.

00:00:50.872 --> 00:00:53.508
You're creating a starvation reflex,

00:00:53.508 --> 00:00:56.092
and it'll actually cause more fat storing.

00:00:56.092 --> 00:00:59.650
One of the triggering effects
of fat storing hormones

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:02.050
is starvation, or going on a diet,

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:05.699
or being hungry 'cause
you're not eating correctly.

00:01:05.699 --> 00:01:07.633
That's why, I think, people
will say sometimes, like

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:10.380
"Oh, yeah, you have to eat
like seven meals a day," or

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:11.588
"You have to keep eating more.

00:01:11.588 --> 00:01:14.422
"I'm actually gaining weight
'cause I'm not eating enough."

00:01:14.422 --> 00:01:16.949
Well, that may or may not be true.

00:01:16.949 --> 00:01:18.624
It really has to do with,
are you eating enough

00:01:18.624 --> 00:01:20.230
nutrients in the calories.

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:21.787
Because, what we don't want to--

00:01:21.787 --> 00:01:24.119
Basically be starving
your body, all right?

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:27.228
What you want, a small amount of protein

00:01:27.228 --> 00:01:28.720
anything excess, like, let's say

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:32.242
10 or even maybe sometimes, even,

00:01:32.242 --> 00:01:34.497
nine, 10, 11, 12, 13,

00:01:34.497 --> 00:01:37.497
up to 17 ounces of protein per meal,

00:01:38.415 --> 00:01:40.037
you go to this restaurant
and they have all

00:01:40.037 --> 00:01:44.204
this protein, that can trigger
the fat storing hormones

00:01:45.423 --> 00:01:46.793
and prevent any chance for weight loss.

00:01:46.793 --> 00:01:48.386
Just because protein triggers fat burning,

00:01:48.386 --> 00:01:51.103
doesn't mean you can have a lot of it.

00:01:51.103 --> 00:01:52.791
Now, the quality is
important, too, because

00:01:52.791 --> 00:01:54.384
is you start doing like this

00:01:54.384 --> 00:01:55.950
soy protein isolate powders,

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.609
which is in a lot of the
diet pre-packaged foods,

00:01:58.609 --> 00:02:00.151
that's not high quality.

00:02:00.151 --> 00:02:01.401
It may trigger the fat storing,

00:02:01.401 --> 00:02:03.063
but it comes with the package.

00:02:03.063 --> 00:02:04.039
It has a lot of side effects.

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:05.410
It might create tumors in the liver.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:08.134
It might make you look
old as you lose weight.

00:02:08.134 --> 00:02:10.729
It's not the best quality
to replace your body tissue,

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:11.814
so I don't recommend it.

00:02:11.814 --> 00:02:16.662
In fact, I don't recommend
a lot of protein powders

00:02:16.662 --> 00:02:19.517
that are with the whey or the soy.

00:02:19.517 --> 00:02:22.179
Egg protein, pea protein,
any of the vegetarian

00:02:22.179 --> 00:02:25.387
protein powders are better,
but I'd prefer if you have

00:02:25.387 --> 00:02:26.692
actual food.

00:02:26.692 --> 00:02:29.582
Then, we're gonna get into
this thing called fats here.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:32.937
Fat, believe it or not, even
though it has more calories,

00:02:32.937 --> 00:02:36.703
it's neutral when it comes
down to the fat storing

00:02:36.703 --> 00:02:37.916
or fat burning.

00:02:37.916 --> 00:02:39.783
In other words, having
butter, for example,

00:02:39.783 --> 00:02:41.341
won't necessarily just turn into

00:02:41.341 --> 00:02:43.674
your hips or stomach weight.

00:02:45.612 --> 00:02:46.445
It's neutral.

00:02:46.445 --> 00:02:48.625
However, when you have certain fats like

00:02:48.625 --> 00:02:50.708
greasy, deep fried foods,

00:02:52.221 --> 00:02:55.262
that grease can affect your liver

00:02:55.262 --> 00:02:56.425
and

00:02:56.425 --> 00:02:57.632
block

00:02:57.632 --> 00:03:00.264
the fat burning process because
all the fat burning hormones

00:03:00.264 --> 00:03:01.902
work through the liver.

00:03:01.902 --> 00:03:04.404
Even though it's an indirect effect,

00:03:04.404 --> 00:03:07.051
you need a healthy liver to burn fat.

00:03:07.051 --> 00:03:09.313
So, we don't want to clog up
the liver with too much fat,

00:03:09.313 --> 00:03:13.054
but some neutral, healthy
fats are totally fine.

00:03:13.054 --> 00:03:14.242
Coconut oil.

00:03:14.242 --> 00:03:15.769
I'm not saying go out
of your way to eat them,

00:03:15.769 --> 00:03:17.817
but don't worry about avoiding them.

00:03:17.817 --> 00:03:19.204
Butter is not a bad thing.

00:03:19.204 --> 00:03:23.033
Safflower oil, sunflower oil, peanut oil,

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:26.126
all that is totally
fine, but the problem is

00:03:26.126 --> 00:03:30.058
doing the fast food
fats that they would do

00:03:30.058 --> 00:03:32.678
in the big vats where you
have hydrogenated oils

00:03:32.678 --> 00:03:35.567
and all this corn oil
and things like that.

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:37.783
OK, so not we got the carbs, all right?

00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:40.566
Now, this is interesting, because

00:03:40.566 --> 00:03:42.316
in one of the premier

00:03:43.365 --> 00:03:45.417
physiology books in all

00:03:45.417 --> 00:03:47.000
medical schools and

00:03:48.108 --> 00:03:51.048
